 domain, and if VIOLATED, what concrete input in the domain mechanically violates it (i.e. sorted merge output contains intervals i before j with i.end >= j.start)?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"No verdict or candidate violating input exists yet in the evidence state; the claim's truth depends on the exact comparison operator used in merge.py, which no artifact in the package has yet exercised against the boundary classes of the domain.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A verdict (HOLDS or VIOLATED) together with, on VIOLATED, a concrete in-domain input list and a mechanical demonstration: the trace of merge on that input and the specific output pair (i, j) with i.end >= j.start after sorting.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"On VIOLATED, the violating input must lie inside the stated domain (<= 6 intervals, integer endpoints in [-10, 10], start <= end) and must mechanically violate the claim as stated (task requirement E-C).\",\n        \"The demonstration must follow the actual code of package/artifacts/merge.py, not an idealized merge; no authorship restriction is imposed on E-C itself.\",\n        \"Deterministic root verification decides whether the demonstration in fact violates the claim.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n        \"E-C\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"Q1\",\n        \"Q3\"\n      ],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"question\": \"Has a systematic search of the domain for a violating input been carried out by a party other than the author of the provisional answer (or has such a party argued that no violating input exists)?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"No second party exists yet in the evidence state: every present artifact was supplied with the package, and any process that reads the package and the claim immediately forms a provisional answer, making itself the author whose search E-B rules inadmissible.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A record of a systematic search over the domain (e.g. structured enumeration of the boundary classes, or exhaustive/bounded enumeration of small interval lists) produced by a process that is not the author of the provisional verdict; on a HOLDS outcome, that party's argument that no violating input exists in the domain.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"Task requirement E-B: the search must be 'carried out by a party other than the author of the provisional answer, or such a party's argument that no violating input exists in the domain'.\",\n        \"The searching party must therefore be a separately launched process: either one that sees the provisional answer but did not author it, or one causally isolated from the worker's conclusions that searches unanchored.\",\n        \"The search record must survive its originating session and be integrated into the deliverable by the governed root step to count.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n        \"E-B\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        \"Q1\"\n      ],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": false,\n        \"requires_isolation\": true,\n        \"contamination\": true,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": true\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","numLines":76,"startLine":1,"totalLines":76}}}
